{"id":"NCT06756607","title":"The ECOG-ACRIN SUPPORT Trial: Multilevel Intervention to Improve Diverse Enrollment in Cancer Clinical Trials","official":"The ECOG-ACRIN SUPPORT Trial: Multilevel Intervention to Improve Diverse Enrollment in Cancer Clinical Trials","summary":"The purpose of this study is to conduct a Hybrid Type 1 cluster-randomized, roll-out effectiveness-implementation trial in NCORP community oncology practice sites (N= 500 Black and Latino cancer patients) to evaluate the effectiveness of the EA SUPPORT intervention combining CT navigators and CT research literacy tools in improving Black and Latino patient referral and accrual to NCI-supported CTs (primary outcomes) and participant and provider awareness and knowledge of CTs (secondary outcomes) while assessing implementation factors. Also, with the CUSP2CT data, Evaluation, and Coordinating Center, conduct final site evaluation and disseminate the SUPPORT intervention to NCORP community oncology sites, research bases, and affiliated trial networks.","conditions":["Cancer"],"interventions":[{"type":"OTHER","name":"SUPPORT toolkit"}],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\nParticipant must be ≥ 18 years of age. Participant must self-identify as Black and/or Latino. Participant must be an oncology patient at a participating NCORP. Participant must be eligible to participate in an ECOG-ACRIN clinical trial. Participant must have the ability to understand and the willingness to sign a e-consent document.\n\nParticipant must be receiving care at a participating NCORP affiliated community oncology site.\n\nParticipant must be English or Spanish speaking to be eligible. Participant must have access to a landline, smartphone, computer, or tablet.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n\\-","minAge":"18 Years","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"INTERVENTIONAL","purpose":"OTHER","enrollment":500,"start":"2025-04-25","pcd":"2027-08-01","upd":"2026-09-14","sponsor":"Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group","areas":["oncology"],"central":["Melissa A Simon, MD, MPH · (312) 503-8780 · m-simon2@northwestern.edu","Elyse R Park, PhD, MPH · (617) 724-6836 · epark@mgh.harvard.edu"],"sites":[{"f":"NEA Baptist Memorial Hospital and Fowler Family Cancer Center - Jonesboro","city":"Jonesboro","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72401","s":"R","lat":35.8423,"lon":-90.7043,"c":"Site Public Contact · 870-936-7066 · Emily.Carvell@bmhcc.org"},{"f":"Liberty County Cancer Care","city":"Hinesville","pr":"Georgia","zip":"31313","s":"R","lat":31.8469,"lon":-81.596,"c":"Site Public Contact · 912-819-5704 · Oncologyresearch@sjchs.org"},{"f":"Regional Cancer Care - Jessup","city":"Jesup","pr":"Georgia","zip":"31545","s":"R","lat":31.6078,"lon":-81.8863,"c":"Site Public Contact · 912-819-5704 · Oncologyresearch@sjchs.org"},{"f":"Lewis Cancer and Research Pavilion at Saint Joseph's/Candler","city":"Savannah","pr":"Georgia","zip":"31405","s":"R","lat":32.0835,"lon":-81.0998,"c":"Site Public Contact · 912-819-5704 · underberga@sjchs.org"},{"f":"Rush-Copley Medical Center","city":"Aurora","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60504","s":"R","lat":41.7606,"lon":-88.3201,"c":"Site Public Contact · 630-978-6212 · RCMC_Cancer_Research@rush.edu"},{"f":"Advocate Good Shepherd Hospital","city":"Barrington","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60010","s":"R","lat":42.1539,"lon":-88.1362,"c":"Site Public Contact · 847-842-4847"},{"f":"Carle BroMenn Outpatient Center","city":"Bloomington","pr":"Illinois","zip":"61704","s":"R","lat":40.4842,"lon":-88.9937,"c":"Site Public Contact · 800-446-5532 · Research@Carle.com"},{"f":"Advocate Illinois Masonic Medical Center","city":"Chicago","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60657","s":"R","lat":41.85,"lon":-87.65,"c":"Site Public Contact · 773-296-5360"},{"f":"AMG Crystal Lake - Oncology","city":"Crystal Lake","pr":"Illinois","zip":"60014","s":"R","lat":42.2411,"lon":-88.3162,"c":"Site Public Contact · 630-929-6129 · advocateresearch@advocate.com"},{"f":"Carle at The Riverfront","city":"Danville","pr":"Illinois","zip":"61832",